{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q133145","formula":"C₂H₂","hill":"C2H2","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":2.0},"names":{"en":"Acetylene","ru":"Ацетилен","uk":"Ацетилен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Acetylene (systematic name: ethyne) is a chemical compound with the formula C2H2 and structure HC≡CH. It is a hydrocarbon and the simplest alkyne. This colorless gas is widely used as a fuel and a chemical building block. It is unstable in its pure form and thus is usually handled as a solution.","ru":"Ацетиле́н (от лат. acetum — «уксус», эти́н, химическая формула — C2H2 или HC ≡ CH) — органическое соединение, возглавляющее класс непредельных углеводородов — алкинов. При нормальных условиях, ацетилен — это бесцветный, слаботоксичный, очень горючий и взрывоопасный газ.","uk":"Ацетиле́н (етин) — органічна сполука, перший представник ряду алкінів. Безбарвний газ, без запаху, легший за повітря."},"fame":77,"pubchemCid":6326,"mass":26.04,"charge":0,"smiles":"C#C","inchikey":"HSFWRNGVRCDJHI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"acetylene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6326","atoms":4,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.6,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.6,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.665,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":1.665,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,3],[0,2,1],[1,3,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q133145","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acetylene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%86%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%86